{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-64181" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution of the exact differential equation\n\n$$\n2xy\\,\\text{d}x+({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\text{d}y=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5d30350a1f3336fa44944ed9d7ee7a88167590ea50237437c789332f365c5ea"} {"question" "q-64181" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the differential equation is of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x,y)=2xy$ and $Q(x,y)={x}^{2}-{y}^{2}.$\n\nSince the equation is exact, our solution $u(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂u}{∂x}=P(x,y),\\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y}=Q(x,y)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\int 2xy\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}y+f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$  Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}+g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\ng(x)=0,\\,f(y)=-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}=c.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5d30350a1f3336fa44944ed9d7ee7a88167590ea50237437c789332f365c5ea"} {"question" "q-64181" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7e7c2b23c58715f0d47af8d9d6e8fb3be8ceba236c15433cd9369e3daa7be111"} {"question" "q-64181" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5d30350a1f3336fa44944ed9d7ee7a88167590ea50237437c789332f365c5ea"} {"question" "q-64181" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{x}^{2}y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}=c"] ["math" "3{x}^{2}-{y}^{3}=c"] ["math" "xy-{y}^{3}=c"] ["math" "{x}^{2}-{y}^{3}=c"] ["math" "{x}^{2}y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}=c"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5d30350a1f3336fa44944ed9d7ee7a88167590ea50237437c789332f365c5ea"} {"question" "q-64181" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{2}y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}=c"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5d30350a1f3336fa44944ed9d7ee7a88167590ea50237437c789332f365c5ea"} {"question" "q-64183" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution of the exact differential equation\n\n$$\n(3{x}^{2}y-3)\\,\\text{d}x+({x}^{3}+{e}^{y})\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nwith the initial condition $y(1)=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5d30350a1f3336fa44944ed9d7ee7a88167590ea50237437c789332f365c5ea"} {"question" "q-64183" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the differential equation is of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x,y)=3{x}^{2}y-3$ and $Q(x,y)={x}^{3}+{e}^{y}.$\n\nSince the equation is exact, our solution $u(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂u}{∂x}=P(x,y),\\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y}=Q(x,y)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\int 3{x}^{2}y-3\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & ={x}^{3}y-3x+f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$  Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{3}+{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & ={x}^{3}y+{e}^{y}+g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\ng(x)=-3x,\\,f(y)={e}^{y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}y-3x+{e}^{y}=c.\n$$\n\nThe particular solution specified by the initial condition must have $y=0$ when $x=1.$ These values determine the value of the constant $c.$ Substituting this into the equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}y-3x+{e}^{y}=c \\\\ (1)^{3}(0)-3(1)+{e}^{0}=c \\\\ -3+1=c \\\\ c=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}y-3x+{e}^{y}=-2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5d30350a1f3336fa44944ed9d7ee7a88167590ea50237437c789332f365c5ea"} {"question" "q-64183" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7e7c2b23c58715f0d47af8d9d6e8fb3be8ceba236c15433cd9369e3daa7be111"} {"question" "q-64183" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5d30350a1f3336fa44944ed9d7ee7a88167590ea50237437c789332f365c5ea"} {"question" "q-64183" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x{y}^{3}-3x=-3"] ["math" "{x}^{2}y+3{x}^{3}+{e}^{2y}=4"] ["math" "{x}^{2}{y}^{2}-{e}^{x-1}+{e}^{y}=0"] ["math" "{x}^{3}y-3x+{e}^{y}=-2"] ["math" "{x}^{3}y-3{e}^{y}=-3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5d30350a1f3336fa44944ed9d7ee7a88167590ea50237437c789332f365c5ea"} {"question" "q-64183" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{3}y-3x+{e}^{y}=-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5d30350a1f3336fa44944ed9d7ee7a88167590ea50237437c789332f365c5ea"} {"question" "q-103178" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following differential equation:\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nGiven that the differential equation is exact, which of the following functions could be $P(x,y)?$\n\n- $y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-y$\n- $xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$\n- $y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5d30350a1f3336fa44944ed9d7ee7a88167590ea50237437c789332f365c5ea"} {"question" "q-103178" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're given $Q(x,y)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy).$ \n\nFirst, let's differentiate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\n$$\n\nNow, let's apply $\\frac{∂}{∂y}$ to each of the given options:\n\n- First, we check $P(x,y)=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-y.$ This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-1\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-y$ does *not* give an exact equation.\n\n- Next, we check $P(x,y)=xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-{x}^{2}y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$ does *not* give an exact equation.\n\n- Finally, we check $P(x,y)=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$  gives an exact equation.\n\nHence, the correct answer is ''III only''." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5d30350a1f3336fa44944ed9d7ee7a88167590ea50237437c789332f365c5ea"} {"question" "q-103178" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7e7c2b23c58715f0d47af8d9d6e8fb3be8ceba236c15433cd9369e3daa7be111"} {"question" "q-103178" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5d30350a1f3336fa44944ed9d7ee7a88167590ea50237437c789332f365c5ea"} {"question" "q-103178" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "ÍII only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5d30350a1f3336fa44944ed9d7ee7a88167590ea50237437c789332f365c5ea"} {"question" "q-103178" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "ÍII only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5d30350a1f3336fa44944ed9d7ee7a88167590ea50237437c789332f365c5ea"} {"question" "q-318629" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following differential equations is exact?  \n\n- $({x}^{2}+y)\\,\\text{d}x+(xy+2)\\,\\text{d}y=0$\n- $(3xy)\\,\\text{d}x+({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y=0$\n- $(6y-x)\\,\\text{d}y-(y-4x)\\,\\text{d}x=0$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5d30350a1f3336fa44944ed9d7ee7a88167590ea50237437c789332f365c5ea"} {"question" "q-318629" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider each equation:\n\n- The first equation is\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+y)\\,\\text{d}x+(xy+2)\\,\\text{d}y=0.\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, the functions $P$ and $Q$ are\n\n$$\nP(x,y)={x}^{2}+y,\\,Q(x,y)=xy+2.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+y) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy+2) \\\\  & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\\,\\times \n$$\n\n \nThus, equation I is not exact.\n\n- The second equation is\n\n$$\n(3xy)\\,\\text{d}x+({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the functions $P$ and $Q$ are\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=3xy,\\,Q(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3xy) \\\\  & =3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nThus, equation II is not exact.\n\n- The third equation is\n\n$$\n(6y-x)\\,\\text{d}y-(y-4x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the functions $P$ and $Q$ are\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=-(y-4x)=4x-y,\\,Q(x,y)=6y-x.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4x-y) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(6y-x) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSo,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\\,✓\n$$\n\nThus, equation III is exact.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5d30350a1f3336fa44944ed9d7ee7a88167590ea50237437c789332f365c5ea"} {"question" "q-318629" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7e7c2b23c58715f0d47af8d9d6e8fb3be8ceba236c15433cd9369e3daa7be111"} {"question" "q-318629" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5d30350a1f3336fa44944ed9d7ee7a88167590ea50237437c789332f365c5ea"} {"question" "q-318629" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5d30350a1f3336fa44944ed9d7ee7a88167590ea50237437c789332f365c5ea"} {"question" "q-318629" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5d30350a1f3336fa44944ed9d7ee7a88167590ea50237437c789332f365c5ea"} {"question" "q-320578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution of the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{22+{x}^{3}{y}^{4}}{\\,13y-{x}^{4}{y}^{3}\\,}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5d30350a1f3336fa44944ed9d7ee7a88167590ea50237437c789332f365c5ea"} {"question" "q-320578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We start by rewriting this equation in differential form.\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nStarting from \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{22+{x}^{3}{y}^{4}}{13y-{x}^{4}{y}^{3}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe first multiply through by $(13y-{x}^{4}{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x$:\n\n$$\n(13y-{x}^{4}{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y=(22+{x}^{3}{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThen, we rearrange the terms:\n\n$$\n(22+{x}^{3}{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x+(22+{x}^{3}{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nNow, we should check for exactness. A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nFor our differential equation, we have\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=22+{x}^{3}{y}^{4},\\,Q(x,y)={x}^{4}{y}^{3}-13y.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\,(22+{x}^{3}{y}^{4}) \\\\  & =\\,4{x}^{3}{y}^{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\,(x\\,(xy)^{3}-13y) \\\\  & =\\,4{x}^{3}{y}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\\,✓\n$$\n\n \nThus, our equation is exact.\n\nSince the equation is exact, our solution $u(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂u}{∂x}=P(x,y),\\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y}=Q(x,y)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\int (22+{x}^{3}{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =22x+\\frac{{x}^{4}{y}^{4}}{4}+f(y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$  Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\int ({x}^{4}{y}^{3}-13y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}{y}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{13}{2}{y}^{2}+g(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\ng(x)=22x,\\,f(y)=-\\frac{13}{2}{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{4}{y}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{13}{2}{y}^{2}+22x=c.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5d30350a1f3336fa44944ed9d7ee7a88167590ea50237437c789332f365c5ea"} {"question" "q-320578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7e7c2b23c58715f0d47af8d9d6e8fb3be8ceba236c15433cd9369e3daa7be111"} {"question" "q-320578" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5d30350a1f3336fa44944ed9d7ee7a88167590ea50237437c789332f365c5ea"} {"question" "q-320578" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{{x}^{4}{y}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{13}{2}{y}^{2}+22x=c"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{4}{y}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{13}{2}{y}^{2}-22x=c"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{4}{y}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{13}{2}{x}^{2}+22x=c"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{4}{y}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{13}{2}{y}^{2}+22x=c"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{4}{y}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{13}{2}{y}^{2}+22y=c"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5d30350a1f3336fa44944ed9d7ee7a88167590ea50237437c789332f365c5ea"} {"question" "q-320578" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{4}{y}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{13}{2}{y}^{2}+22x=c"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070079/state.json" "file_sha256" "a5d30350a1f3336fa44944ed9d7ee7a88167590ea50237437c789332f365c5ea"}] "usage" {"q-64181" []} "basis" 2442 "retractions" [[17592186148070 :question/problem "Find the general solution of the exact differential equation\n\n$2xydx + (x^{2} 